title: Paradigm symbols pass (4 aspects) + University pack expanded to 9 tracks/53 entries
summary: 'Two-pronged knowledge-capture pass on the now-mature atelier, both via the Paradigm MCP. (1) SYMBOLS: atelier had 151 components but ZERO aspects — registered the 4 multi-site cross-cutting invariants with enforced code anchors via paradigm_purpose_add_aspect: ~layer-tag-isolation (4 anchors), ~detected-vs-user-edited (2), ~copy-on-write-doc (5), ~source-tagged-mutation (6). Skipped ~schema-validated-mutation after research proved it single-site (only document.ts validates). Fixed a YAML parse error in packages/canvas/.purpose. aspects 0→4, 180 symbols, root .purpose validates clean, all anchors resolve. (2) UNIVERSITY PACK: was stuck at v0.1.0 (4 tracks/24 entries) while 4 releases shipped. Refreshed 001/201/301 (tool count 52/51→61, MCP groups 13→15 adding recipe+import, fixed stale ''atelier export''→export-image/render commands), then authored 5 new tracks via 5 parallel file-write-only builders (no index race): ATEL-401 (state machines/motion), 501 (video pipeline, teaches the detected-vs-user-edited + layer-tag-isolation aspects), 601 (recipes/overlays/carousel), 701 (export/delivery), 801 (studio + live agent loop, teaches source-tagged-mutation). Central verification caught + fixed a stray </content> artifact in one note and a phantom reindex-trigger entry in index.yaml. validate --project: 53 items, all checks passed. Pack now 9 tracks/53 entries.'
