commit: a060347
learnings:
  - Aspects must be MULTI-SITE cross-cutting rules (N>1 enforcement anchors that stay in sync); single-site invariants (resolveFrame determinism
  - SaveCoordinator) belong in the component's .purpose description
  - not as aspects — confirmed via advisor + research. paradigm_purpose_add_aspect requires real code anchors; declaring cross-package aspects in the ROOT .purpose with repo-relative anchor paths works cleanly. University pack authoring parallelizes safely ONLY if builders are file-write-only (no paradigm university CLI) — the shared index.yaml races otherwise; orchestrator does ONE central reindex+validate. The index rebuild (via the add-note trick) structurally lags by one note
  - leaving a phantom entry; there's no clean university reindex subcommand
  - 'so hand-edit index.yaml + totalContent to match disk. Quiz YAML: single-quote any string with a colon-space or braces or the entry silently fails to index (bit multiple builders).'
